/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/Fumar.dat -- ONE model species, ONE typed file: the doubly charged anion of fumaric acid.

  NO `aqueousThermo` ON PURPOSE.  The ionisation (pK, dH, dCp) of fumaric acid is evaluated in
  Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049, Table 6 (Ionization data for some Krebs compounds), p. 1057, and is in chemistry/ -- so the SPECIATION (pH, distribution) is complete.  No work
  in hand prints a formation enthalpy or entropy of this aqueous ion, so a balance that needs its
  enthalpy REFUSES BY NAME instead of borrowing a value.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    Fumar;
formula     "C4H2O4-2";
charge  -2;
MW { value 114.056; unit g/mol;}
